# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 3 (stage A, 2026-10-18). Each life event below gets a first bold way,
# sometimes a second, and the first bold way's two links (well and badly), each with its own bold way.
# Syntax: header of build.py; design: bold-ways brief.

# ================================================================ a friend for life

== bold: a friend for life / B
base: go into a venture together, and share the risk and the profit
likelier_if: has [striking a deal] +5; has [selling] +5; mark 'took a wild risk' +5
- B | put your savings in with theirs, and open a business under both your names | v: achievement, power | act: put their savings in with the friend's, and open a business under both their names | chance: 35 | requires: savings | grants: business partner | takes_if_fails: savings
works: {N} and {friend} sign a lease together, and by the end of the year both their names are over the door and trade is steady.
works: {friend} turns out to be the partner {N} needed, and the two of them share the risk and the profit as they promised.
fails: The business never finds its customers, and {Ns} savings go with it before the year is out.
fails: {N} and {friend} close the shop with nothing left in the bank, and {N} starts again from an empty account.

== an offer for the business you share
tier: link
of_bold: a friend for life / B
side: well
delay: 1-2
holds: business partner
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-100
stakes: .7
tone: mixed
life: work, friends, money
horizon: months
roles: friend
earth: a bigger firm offers to buy the business you built with your friend
scene: A bigger firm has made an offer for the business {N} and {friend} built together. The money is good, but {friend} says selling would feel like selling the friendship.
scene gone: {friend} has moved away and left {N} to run the business alone. Now a bigger firm makes an offer, and {friend} writes from far off that whatever {N} decides is fine.
- W | keep to the deed you both signed, and sell only if you both agree | v: conformity, benevolence | act: keep to the deed they both signed, and sell only if both agree | chance: 80
- U | have the business valued properly before anyone gives an answer | v: self-direction, security | chance: 78
- B | press your friend to sell, and hold out for the top price | v: power, achievement | act: press the friend to sell, and hold out for the top price | chance: 65
- R | turn the offer down on the spot, and take your friend out to celebrate | v: stimulation, benevolence | act: turn the offer down on the spot, and take the friend out to celebrate | chance: 82
- G | keep the business as it is, small and your own | v: tradition, security | act: keep the business as it is, small and their own | chance: 75
works: The answer is given, and {N} and {friend} go back to work as partners.
works: The offer passes, and the business is steadier for knowing what it is worth.
fails: The talks drag on for months, and the partners say things they later regret.
fails: The firm opens a rival shop down the road, and trade thins for a season.
works gone: The answer is given, and {N} goes back to running the business, with the old friend's blessing from afar.
works gone: The offer passes, and the business is steadier for knowing what it is worth.
fails gone: The talks drag on for months, and the letters to the old friend grow short and tense.
fails gone: The firm opens a rival shop down the road, and trade thins for a season.

== bold: an offer for the business you share / R
base: turn the offer down on the spot, and take your friend out to celebrate
likelier_if: years [business partner] 2 +5; has [good credit] +5
- R | turn the firm down, and sign for a second shop the same week | v: stimulation, achievement | act: turn the firm down, and sign for a second shop the same week | chance: 40 | requires: business partner | grants: premises of one's own | takes_if_fails: business partner
works: {N} and {friend} sign the lease on a second shop, the very premises the bigger firm wanted for itself.
works: The second shop fills from the first week, and the premises are theirs to keep.
fails: The second shop drains the first, and {friend} pulls out of the partnership in the spring.
fails: The two of them quarrel over the lease, and the partnership ends with {friend} selling up.
works gone: {N} signs the lease on a second shop, the very premises the bigger firm wanted for itself.
works gone: The second shop fills from the first week, and the premises are {Ns} to keep.
fails gone: The second shop drains the first, and the old friend writes from far off to end the partnership.
fails gone: A quarrel by letter over the lease ends the partnership, and the old friend's share is sold.

